@*
  The frame a role dashboard draws its cards in, on Home (T335, flow 01; R2-Landing-Loading, R2-Landing-Error; review
  S22(c); T329). DESIGN.md § Dashboard page.

  - Loading: the grid and its cards at once, each card its title and a skeleton (DashboardCard's IsLoading), and the grid
    marked busy. Nothing is offered until the read returns. A status says so, "Loading your Home." (T350, flow 04, C11):
    the region is on the page from the first render, empty once the read has answered, so its words are announced when
    they come rather than arriving with a region a screen reader has not yet seen.
  - Failed: one danger Alert with fixed words and Try again, which reads again, and no cards: a card drawn empty would say
    there is nothing, and one drawn as a skeleton would say it is still coming. The failure's own text is the log's, not
    the page's.
  - Otherwise: the grid and its cards.

  Try again is an action whose button goes with the alert, so its answer (the cards, or the alert again) takes the focus
  once it has come (ActionResult; DESIGN.md § Button system, T234): the region that replaces the error (C10 e).
*@
<p class="visually-hidden" role="status">@(IsLoading ? LoadingWords : null)</p>
<ActionResult @ref="_result">
  @if (Failed)
  {
    <Alert Kind="danger">
      <div class="alert-row">
        <span class="alert-row-text"><strong>Could not load your Home.</strong> Nothing has changed. Try again, or come back in a few minutes.</span>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" @onclick="RetryAsync">
          <Icon Name="refresh-cw" />
          Try again
        </button>
      </div>
    </Alert>
  }
  else
  {
    <div class="dashboard-grid" aria-busy="@(IsLoading ? "true" : null)">
      @ChildContent
    </div>
  }
</ActionResult>

@code {
  /// <summary>What the status says while the dashboard reads (T350, C11; R3-Spec § 1, Loading).</summary>
  public const string LoadingWords = "Loading your Home.";

  private ActionResult? _result;

  /// <summary>The dashboard's read has not returned yet.</summary>
  [Parameter] public bool IsLoading { get; set; }

  /// <summary>The dashboard's read failed: the page says so once, and offers to read again.</summary>
  [Parameter] public bool Failed { get; set; }

  /// <summary>Reads the dashboard again; it returns once the read has answered.</summary>
  [Parameter] public EventCallback OnRetry { get; set; }

  [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;

  private async Task RetryAsync()
  {
    await OnRetry.InvokeAsync();
    _result?.FocusAfterRender();
  }
}
